              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sarah Jo"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Most excellent.\n\nI made one as the recipe stated, and with the second, I added half an ounce \nof irish creme. Smooth, but with a bite.\nI could see myself becoming friendly with these quite often. ;)"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Katie Davis"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is a white russian (coffee liqueur = kahlua). I've made a few espresso martinis in my day, though, and can say that the best way is: shot of espresso, vanilla vodka, and kahlua (or whatever sweetened coffe-ish liqueur you prefer). If you like yours creamy, add Baileys (although I tried it once with Amarula, and my oh my it was tasty! So, really, a creamy liqueur of your preference). ... and like with many martinis... shake that thing till you can't shake any more - a frothy beverage is a good one.",
            "datePublished": "2009-07-21T12:50:15.700Z"
          },
